-- title:
--   Places of K(j,j_q) lift to ℚ̄(X₀(q))
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number assumed prime, let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$, and write $F_0 =$ `fieldOver (1 * q) K` for the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ (Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) generated by the constant series attached to the elements of $K$ together with the two series `jqModC` (the $q$-expansion $t^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator series of }j)$) and `jqNModC` at level $1\cdot q$ (its substitution $t\mapsto t^{q}$). Let $V$ be a place of $F_0$ over $K$, i.e. a proper valuation subring of $F_0$ that contains the image of $K$ and is a principal ideal ring. The assertion is that there exists a place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — where this field is the intermediate field generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q((t))$ adjoined to $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions at level $1\cdot q$ — such that $W$, regarded as a place over the smaller constant field $K$ and then contracted along the inclusion of $F_0$, has valuation ring exactly that of $V$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the classical theory of extension of places in a separable constant-field extension of a function field (Chevalley, Deuring): every place of the number-field level $K(j,j_q)$ arises from a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(q))$. It is used in the analysis of the nodes on the reduction of $X_0(q)$, specifically by [`ModularCurve.exists_place_centred_node_of_height_one_of_natCast_notMem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_place_centred_node_of_height_one_of_natCast_notMem); no particular choice of $W$ is asserted.
